     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Â©FAO. Editorial use only. Photo credit must be given</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:rights>
   <dc:description>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">11 May 2016, Muguga, Kenya - Scientists take an inventory of frozen specimens of the rinderpest causing pathogens 11, May 2016 set to be destroyed at the Biotechnology Research Institute situated at the Muguga KALRO Campus in Kiambu county, Kenya. Destroying virus samples kept in laboratory freezers, one-third of which are storing them at biosecurity level 2 â€” too low,  is seen as a critical step in ensuring that a disease that took years to eradicate remains gone.</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:description>
